{
  "id": "ue_drift_anticipation_v2",
  "description": "Anticipation over the four coding-SFT interventions actually trained in Phase 1 (writing C#, Go, Rust, PHP on the executable-verified competitive-programming pools, which replaced the retired Magicoder arms), forecasting cross-domain spillover onto the full Utility-Engineering preference battery. Anchors are the four trained interventions, identical to coding_drift_anticipation_v2. Targets are ALL 81 UE options, so there is no target selection and nothing to pre-freeze: a forecast exists for whatever UE preference turns out to drift, and forecasting only the items seen to drift would select on the outcome and bias alpha. UE is measured per-option at every checkpoint, so each item's pre/post utility is a directly-measured ground truth. Ternary MORE/LESS/SAME, dataset-description level only (the concreteness sweep is reserved for the trained tasks, as in the coding arm). Separate from coding_drift_anticipation_v2 so the coding battery is untouched. Generated from ue_options_subset.json.",
